<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 8 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Capitals of the World</h1><p class="path-tagline">Eight cities where power lived.</p><p class="path-intro">Every age has a city where the world's business seems to be decided. This path walks through eight of them at their height, from the gates of Babylon to the lakes of Tenochtitlan, asking what made each the centre of its world and what remains.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Builder</a> · <a href="/start">the Navigator</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/babylon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babylon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Babylon</span><span class="path-step-why">Gate of the gods: the ancient world's byword for the great city.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/rome"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Rome</span><span class="path-step-why">A million people at the centre of the Mediterranean world.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Constantinople</span><span class="path-step-why">The new Rome on the Bosphorus, besieged by everyone and taken almost never.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Baghdad</span><span class="path-step-why">The round city of the caliphs, where the world's learning was translated.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/changan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Chang'an</span><span class="path-step-why">The Tang capital, the largest city on earth and the eastern end of the Silk Road.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba"><span class="path-step-ph">6</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Córdoba</span><span class="path-step-why">Umayyad Córdoba, where al-Andalus outshone every city of Latin Europe.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/cusco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cusco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Cusco</span><span class="path-step-why">The navel of the Inca world, from which the four quarters ran.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Tenochtitlan</span><span class="path-step-why">The island capital on the lake, larger than the European cities of its conquerors.</span></span></a></li></ol>
